{"page_content": "When considering the available dilution, account should be taken of the fluctuating flow rates of typical receiving waters. The low-flow rate (or 10 percentile) should always be used. Where only average flows are available, the flow for dilution purposes should be estimated as one third of this average. When a site-specific assessment is appropriate, the actual dilution factor after complete mixing can be calculated from the flow rate of the river and the effluent discharge rate (this approach should only be used for rivers, not for estuaries or lakes):", "metadata": {"doc_id": "78023268-4865-4b93-b890-3e5ff32c8df3", "content_type": "CompositeElement", "filename": "IR_CSR_R16_V4_FINAL.pdf"}}